  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">A born-in-editor content model with a 1 / 1.1 / 1.1.1 clause tree renders to a .docx whose numbering is a STYLE-LINKED multi-level `w:abstractNum` (ilvl 0-8, `%N` lvlText) referenced via the heading/list styles — NOT literal "1. " text runs and NOT a direct paragraph numId alongside a style numId.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Headings render with real `Heading1..6` paragraph styles; inline formatting renders as `w:b`/`w:i`/`w:u`; tables render as native `w:tbl` — all round-trip through the mammoth import + `ParaIdPreParser` on the next Load.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every emitted `w:p` (incl. table-cell + nested-table paragraphs) carries a unique OOXML-valid `w14:paraId` (mint scheme per `ParaIdPreParser`); a subsequent `ComposeParagraphRedlineSynthesizer` edit finds paragraphs by those paraIds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A born-in-editor first Save (SaveComposeDocumentRequest carries ContentModel, no Content bytes, no DocumentSpeId) persists the server-RENDERED bytes via create-on-save (captured at the SpeFileStore facade) — no client docx.js reconstruction anywhere in the path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A tracked-change edit applied to a rendered doc (via task 022 synthesizer) does not corrupt its numbering (numbering is instance-clean + style-linked at birth).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Services/Compose/` injects no AI-internal type (Tier-1 NetArchTest green); no `Microsoft.Graph` type in the renderer; no new NuGet; publish ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR states the Placement Justification and cites design §11 that server-side render-from-model is deterministic OOXML authoring, NOT an AI dispatch (ADR-039 complied).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

